<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1. </span><math id="S4.T1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP and <math id="S4.T1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n})=R^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n})=R^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n})</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S4.T1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq c(g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq c(g)</annotation></semantics></math>, by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, Theorem 1.4]</cite> and Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm10" title="Theorem 1.10. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.10</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The following is a consequence of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\leq 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\leq 7</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq c(g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq c(g)</annotation></semantics></math> as specified in Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}H^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n})=RH^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}H^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n})=RH^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, if <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is odd and <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq c(g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq c(g)</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}H^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n})=\mathrm{gr}^{W}_{k}H^{k}_{c}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n})=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>gr</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}H^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n})=\mathrm{gr}^{W}_{k}H^{k}_{c}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm9" title="Theorem 1.9. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.9</span></a>, assuming Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the Hard Lefschetz theorem, it suffices to prove that <math id="S4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{k}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,n})^{\mathrm{ss}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ss</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{k}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,n})^{\mathrm{ss}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial in <math id="S4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}_{12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}_{12}</annotation></semantics></math> for fixed <math id="S4.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq 17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq 17</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 11</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the right exact sequence</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{k-2}(\widetilde{\partial\mathcal{M}_{3,n}})\rightarrow H^{k}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,n})\rightarrow W_{k}H^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})\rightarrow 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{k-2}(\widetilde{\partial\mathcal{M}_{3,n}})\rightarrow H^{k}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{3,n})\rightarrow W_{k}H^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})\rightarrow 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, Theorems 1.1, 1.2 and Lemma 2.1]</cite>, for <math id="S4.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\prime}\leq 15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}\leq 15</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{k^{\prime}}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g^{\prime},n^{\prime}})^{\mathrm{ss}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ss</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{k^{\prime}}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g^{\prime},n^{\prime}})^{\mathrm{ss}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial in <math id="S4.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}_{12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}_{12}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="S4.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> as well as for <math id="S4.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}\leq 13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}\leq 13</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since we assume <math id="S4.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 11</annotation></semantics></math>, no <math id="S4.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}\geq 14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}\geq 14</annotation></semantics></math> appears as a factor in a component of the normalized boundary.
It follows that, <math id="S4.p11.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{k-2}(\widetilde{\partial\mathcal{M}_{3,n}})^{\mathrm{ss}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ss</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{k-2}(\widetilde{\partial\mathcal{M}_{3,n}})^{\mathrm{ss}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial in <math id="S4.p11.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p11.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}_{12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}_{12}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, Theorem 1.4]</cite>, <math id="S4.p11.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{3,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{3,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP and <math id="S4.p11.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})=R^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})=R^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.p11.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 11</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S4.p11.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}H^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})=RH^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}H^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})=RH^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})</annotation></semantics></math> by Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>. Hence, <math id="S4.p11.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}H^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}H^{k}(\mathcal{M}_{3,n})</annotation></semantics></math> is pure Hodge–Tate, and the theorem follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>The CKgP in genus 7 with at most 3 marked points</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to prove Theorems <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>, <a href="#S1.Thmthm5" title="Theorem 1.5. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.5</span></a>(<a href="#S1.I1.i3" title="item 3 ‣ Theorem 1.5. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) for <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=14</annotation></semantics></math>, and <a href="#S1.Thmthm7" title="Theorem 1.7. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.7</span></a>, we need more base cases in genus <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>. The required base cases are given by Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm10" title="Theorem 1.10. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.10</span></a>, which we now prove.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In order to prove Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm10" title="Theorem 1.10. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.10</span></a>, we filter <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> by gonality:</p>
<table id="S5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{2}_{7,n}\subset\mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}\subset\mathcal{M}^{4}_{7,n}\subset\mathcal{M}^{5}_{7,n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{2}_{7,n}\subset\mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}\subset\mathcal{M}^{4}_{7,n}\subset\mathcal{M}^{5}_{7,n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{k}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{k}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the locus parametrizing smooth curves <math id="S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> marked points that admit a map of degree at most <math id="S5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Standard results from Brill–Noether theory show that the maximal gonality of a genus <math id="S5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math> curve is <math id="S5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>. By Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>(<a href="#S4.I1.i3" title="item 3 ‣ Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), to show that <math id="S5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP, it suffices to show that each gonality stratum</p>
<table id="S5.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{k}_{7,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}^{k-1}_{7,n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{k}_{7,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}^{k-1}_{7,n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">has the CKgP. Moreover, to show that <math id="S5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{7,n})=R^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{7,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{7,n})=R^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{7,n})</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to show for each <math id="S5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> that all classes supported on <math id="S5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{k}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{k}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> are tautological up to classes
supported on <math id="S5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{k-1}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{k-1}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, we must show that every class in <math id="S5.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{7,n}^{k}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{7,n}^{k-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{7,n}^{k}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{7,n}^{k-1})</annotation></semantics></math>
pushes forward to a class in <math id="S5.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{7,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}^{k-1}_{7,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{7,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}^{k-1}_{7,n})</annotation></semantics></math> that is the restriction of a tautological class
on <math id="S5.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1. </span>Hyperelliptic and trigonal loci</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, Lemma 9.9]</cite>, if <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 14</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP and all classes in <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{7,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{M}_{7,n})</annotation></semantics></math> supported on <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> are tautological. Note that this includes the hyperelliptic locus.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2. </span>The tetragonal locus</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To study the tetragonal locus <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{4}_{7,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{4}_{7,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we will use the Hurwitz stack <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}</annotation></semantics></math> parametrizing degree <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\colon C\rightarrow\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\colon C\rightarrow\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth curve of genus <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> marked points.
There is a forgetful morphism</p>
<table id="S5.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}\colon\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}\rightarrow\mathcal{M}_{g,n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}\colon\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}\rightarrow\mathcal{M}_{g,n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Restricting to curves of gonality exactly <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain a proper morphism</p>
<table id="S5.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}^{\prime}\colon\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}^{\Diamond}:=\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}\smallsetminus\beta_{n}^{-1}(\mathcal{M}^{3}_{g,n})\rightarrow\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}^{3}_{g,n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}^{\prime}\colon\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}^{\Diamond}:=\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}\smallsetminus\beta_{n}^{-1}(\mathcal{M}^{3}_{g,n})\rightarrow\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}^{3}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with image <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{4}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{4}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. To show that <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{4}_{7,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{4}_{7,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP, it suffices to show that <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP by Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>(<a href="#S4.I1.i2" title="item 2 ‣ Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). We will do so by further stratifying <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Section 4.4]</cite>, the first two authors studied a stratification of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,7}:=\mathcal{H}_{4,7,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,7}:=\mathcal{H}_{4,7,0}</annotation></semantics></math> with no markings. Here we carry out a similar analysis with marked points. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> associates to a point in <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> a rank <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and a rank <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, both of degree <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+3</annotation></semantics></math>, equipped with a canonical isomorphism <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det E\cong\det F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det E\cong\det F</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, Section 3]</cite>. Let <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> be the moduli stack of pairs of vector bundles <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+3</annotation></semantics></math>, together with an isomorphism of their determinants as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, Definition 5.2]</cite>. Let <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\colon\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\colon\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> be the universal <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-fibration, and let <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> be the universal bundles on <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. There is a natural morphism <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\to\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\to\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> that sends a degree <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> cover to its associated pair of vector bundles.
Moreover, the Casnati–Ekedahl construction gives an embedding of the universal curve <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the natural commutative diagram</p>
<table id="S5.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.E1.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="72.01" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-35.53px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 236.7 72.01" width="236.7"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,72.01) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(120.92,0) translate(0,35.53)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -115.78 -26.5)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 71.05)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 15.47)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 8.96 0) translate(21.64,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -15.68 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.27em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="17.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E1.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{C}_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{C}_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 68.92 0) translate(51.08,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -11.92 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.72em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="9.99"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E1.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 145.61 0) translate(59.58,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -20.41 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.95em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.4" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="26.98"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E1.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 62.03)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(30.59,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -24.64 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.56em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="35.44"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E1.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 61.19 0) translate(58.82,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -19.65 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.84em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="25.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E1.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{4,g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{H}_{4,g}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 152.28 0) translate(52.91,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -13.74 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.99em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="13.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E1.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{B},}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{B},}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -63.27 23.52 L -14.48 23.52"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -14.2 23.52)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -41.03 26.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.35em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.73" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="4.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E1.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces b}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -85.18 12.64 L -85.18 -11.16"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -85.18 -11.43)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 4.23 14.72 L 4.23 -11.16"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 4.23 -11.43)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 22.38 23.52 L 62.21 23.52"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 62.49 23.52)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 39.57 26.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.43em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.17" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="6"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E1.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces a}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 89.41 14.72 L 89.41 -11.16"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 89.41 -11.43)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -98.69 -11.71 C -105.85 -5.42 -105.58 6.68 -98.57 12.3"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.78033 0.62537 -0.62537 0.78033 -98.36 12.47)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -117.94 -0.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="10.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E1.m1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\sigma_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">σ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\sigma_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -54.31 -23.05 L -22.21 -23.05"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -21.93 -23.05)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 30.11 -23.05 L 68.88 -23.05"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 69.16 -23.05)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the universal curve over <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\circ b\circ\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\circ b\circ\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> sends a pointed curve to the image of the <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th marking under the Casnati–Ekedahl embedding. Taking the product of these maps for <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain a commutative diagram</p>
<table id="S5.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
