</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma 10.5 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>)<span id="S5.Thmthm1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}^{\Diamond})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}^{\Diamond})</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the image of the map <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})\to A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}^{\Diamond})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})\to A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}^{\Diamond})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta^{\prime}_{n*}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}_{n*}x</annotation></semantics></math> is tautological on <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{g,n}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The splitting types of the Casnati–Ekedahl bundles <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> induce a stratification on <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,7}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We write <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=(e_{1},e_{2},e_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=(e_{1},e_{2},e_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=(f_{1},f_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=(f_{1},f_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> to indicate that the bundles have splitting types</p>
<table id="S5.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{2})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{3})\qquad\text{and}\qquad F=\mathcal{O}(f_{1})\oplus\mathcal{O}(f_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{2})\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{3})\qquad\text{and}\qquad F=\mathcal{O}(f_{1})\oplus\mathcal{O}(f_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">We will consider a stratification into three pieces</p>
<table id="S5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}=X_{n}\sqcup Y_{n}\sqcup Z_{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}=X_{n}\sqcup Y_{n}\sqcup Z_{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">The three strata correspond to unions of splitting types of <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>. The possible splitting types are recorded in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Section 4.4]</cite>.
The locus <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of covers with maximally unbalanced splitting types and parametrizes hyperelliptic curves <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Equation 4.5]</cite>. Its image in <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{7,n}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{7,n}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, which has the CKgP when <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 14</annotation></semantics></math>, as noted above. We will show that <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> have the CKgP and that <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> surjects onto the Chow ring of their union, which is <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We start with <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{n}\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{n}\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the locus of covers with splitting types <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=(3,3,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=(3,3,4)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=(5,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=(5,5)</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=(3,3,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=(3,3,4)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=(4,6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=(4,6)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.2</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP and <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})\to A^{*}(X_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})\to A^{*}(X_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=4</annotation></semantics></math> in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, Definition 10.8]</cite>, we have <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{n}=\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{n}=\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. The result then follows from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, Lemmas 10.11 and 10.12]</cite> with <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=7</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=f_{1}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=f_{1}=4</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Now let <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{n}\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{n}\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the union</p>
<table id="S5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{n}=\Sigma_{2,n}\sqcup\Sigma_{3,n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{n}=\Sigma_{2,n}\sqcup\Sigma_{3,n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{2,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{2,n}</annotation></semantics></math> parametrizes covers with splitting types <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=(2,4,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=(2,4,4)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=(4,6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=(4,6)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{3,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{3,n}</annotation></semantics></math> parametrizes covers with splitting types <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=(2,3,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=(2,3,5)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=(4,6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=(4,6)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\colon\mathcal{P}\rightarrow\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\colon\mathcal{P}\rightarrow\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> is the structure map for the <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> bundle <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\colon\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\to\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\colon\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}\to\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the structure map and <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}\colon(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n}\to\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}\colon(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n}\to\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th projection. Define</p>
<table id="S5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}:=\eta_{i}^{*}\gamma^{*}c_{1}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1))\mbox{ \ \  and \ \ }\zeta_{i}:=\eta_{i}^{*}c_{1}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}}(1))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}:=\eta_{i}^{*}\gamma^{*}c_{1}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1))\mbox{ \ \  and \ \ }\zeta_{i}:=\eta_{i}^{*}c_{1}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}}(1)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> generate <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> as an algebra over <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{B})</annotation></semantics></math>. Write <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell}:=\Sigma_{\ell,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell}:=\Sigma_{\ell,0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.3</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=2,3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a surjection</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell})[z_{1},\ldots,z_{n},\zeta_{1},\ldots,\zeta_{n}]\to A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell,n})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell})[z_{1},\ldots,z_{n},\zeta_{1},\ldots,\zeta_{n}]\to A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell,n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">induced by <math id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell,n}\rightarrow\Sigma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell,n}\rightarrow\Sigma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and restriction from <math id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, <math id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{f}</annotation></semantics></math> be the splitting types associated to <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}\subset\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}\subset\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> be the locally closed substack that parametrizes pairs of bundles <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> with locally constant splitting types <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. We write <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}):=\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}):=\mathcal{O}(e_{1})\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathcal{O}(e_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. By construction, <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the preimage of <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> along <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}\to\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}\to\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We therefore study the base change of (<a href="#S5.E2" title="In 5.2. The tetragonal locus ‣ 5. The CKgP in genus 7 with at most 3 marked points ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>) along <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}\to\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}\to\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S5.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.E3.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="81.99" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-41px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 189.12 81.99" width="189.12"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,81.99) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(94.56,0) translate(0,41)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -94.56 -28.93)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 82)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 15.47)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(25.52,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -19.56 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="25.29"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E3.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Sigma_{\ell,n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Sigma_{\ell,n}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 51.04 0) translate(85.65,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -46.48 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.72em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.72em;font-size:10pt;" height="20.37" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="79.12"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E3.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 69.93)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 4.99 0) translate(20.53,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -14.58 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.11em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="15.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E3.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Sigma_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Sigma_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 72.82 0) translate(63.87,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -24.7 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.57em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.51em;font-size:10pt;" height="16.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="35.56"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E3.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}.}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -43.24 28.99 L -11.14 28.99"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -10.86 28.99)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -69.04 16.23 L -69.04 -13.58"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -69.04 -13.86)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 42.13 10.22 L 42.13 -13.58"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 42.13 -13.86)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -48.23 -25.47 L 10.64 -25.47"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.91 -25.47)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now recall the description of <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> as an open substack of a vector bundle on <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}</annotation></semantics></math>, as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Lemma 3.10]</cite>. Let</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subset H^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))=H^{0}(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee},\gamma^{*}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}}(2))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subset H^{0}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\Sym^{2}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))=H^{0}(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee},\gamma^{*}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}}(2))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">be the open subset of equations that define a smooth curve, as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Lemma 3.10]</cite>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell}=[(U\times\mathbb{G}_{m})/\SL_{2}\ltimes(\Aut(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))\times\Aut(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell}=[(U\times\mathbb{G}_{m})/\SL_{2}\ltimes(\Aut(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))\times\Aut(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">The stack <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the part obtained by forgetting <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}=[\mathbb{G}_{m}/\SL_{2}\ltimes(\Aut(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))\times\Aut(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>SL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}=[\mathbb{G}_{m}/\SL_{2}\ltimes(\Aut(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))\times\Aut(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">As explained in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Equation 3.1]</cite>, there is a product of stacks <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\BGL_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>BGL</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\BGL_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> which is an affine bundle over
<math id="S5.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{B}\!\Aut(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{B}\!\Aut(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e}))</annotation></semantics></math>. As such, <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP by Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>(<a href="#S4.I1.i4" title="item 4 ‣ Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.I1.i6" title="item 6 ‣ Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>). It follows that <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> also has the CKgP by Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>(<a href="#S4.I1.i1" title="item 1 ‣ Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.I1.i4" title="item 4 ‣ Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us define the rank <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}:=\gamma^{*}\mathcal{F}^{\vee}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}}(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}:=\gamma^{*}\mathcal{F}^{\vee}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}}(2)</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math>. Write <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the restriction of <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The discussion above says that <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is an open substack of the vector bundle <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi\circ\gamma)_{*}\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi\circ\gamma)_{*}\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we give a similar description with marked points. Consider the evaluation map</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi\circ\gamma)^{*}(\pi\circ\gamma)_{*}\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}\rightarrow\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi\circ\gamma)^{*}(\pi\circ\gamma)_{*}\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}\rightarrow\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Pulling back to the fiber product <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S5.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{j}^{*}(\pi\circ\gamma)^{*}(\pi\circ\gamma)_{*}\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}\rightarrow\bigoplus_{i=1}^{n}\eta_{i}^{*}\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{j}^{*}(\pi\circ\gamma)^{*}(\pi\circ\gamma)_{*}\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}\rightarrow\bigoplus_{i=1}^{n}\eta_{i}^{*}\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{j}^{*}(\pi\circ\gamma)^{*}(\pi\circ\gamma)_{*}\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{j}^{*}(\pi\circ\gamma)^{*}(\pi\circ\gamma)_{*}\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>.
The kernel <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> of (<a href="#S5.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.2. The tetragonal locus ‣ 5. The CKgP in genus 7 with at most 3 marked points ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>) parametrizes tuples of <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> points on <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math> together with a section of</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee},\gamma^{*}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}}(2))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee},\gamma^{*}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}}(2))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">that vanishes on the points. There is therefore a natural map <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell,n}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell,n}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by sending a pointed curve to the images of the points on <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math> and the defining section of the curve. The kernel <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> is not locally free. Nevertheless, its restriction to the open substack <math id="S5.SS2.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{n}\subset(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{n}\subset(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> where (<a href="#S5.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.2. The tetragonal locus ‣ 5. The CKgP in genus 7 with at most 3 marked points ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>) is surjective is locally free.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">We claim that the map <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell,n}\to\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell,n}\to\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> factors through <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}|_{U_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}|_{U_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>. To see this,
suppose <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math> is the vanishing of a section of <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{*}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}}(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{*}\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^{\vee}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^{\vee}}(2)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth and irreducible.
By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, Lemma 10.6]</cite>, if <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, the evaluation map (<a href="#S5.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 5.2. The tetragonal locus ‣ 5. The CKgP in genus 7 with at most 3 marked points ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>) is surjective at any tuple of <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> distinct points on <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that the image of the composition <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell,n}\rightarrow\mathcal{Y}\rightarrow(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell,n}\rightarrow\mathcal{Y}\rightarrow(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="S5.SS2.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell,n}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{Y}|_{U_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell,n}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{Y}|_{U_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">In summary, we have a sequence of maps</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell,n}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{Y}|_{U_{n}}\rightarrow U_{n}\hookrightarrow(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^{n}\rightarrow(\mathcal{P}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^{n}\rightarrow\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell,n}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{Y}|_{U_{n}}\rightarrow U_{n}\hookrightarrow(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^{n}\rightarrow(\mathcal{P}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^{n}\rightarrow\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">each of which is an open inclusion, vector bundle, or product of projective bundles. Since <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP, it follows that <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell,n}</annotation></semantics></math> also has the CKgP by Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>(<a href="#S4.I1.i1" title="item 1 ‣ Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>),(<a href="#S4.I1.i4" title="item 4 ‣ Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), and (<a href="#S4.I1.i5" title="item 5 ‣ Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). Moreover, we see that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}})[z_{1},\ldots,z_{n},\zeta_{1},\ldots,\zeta_{n}]\to A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell,n})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}})[z_{1},\ldots,z_{n},\zeta_{1},\ldots,\zeta_{n}]\to A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell,n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">is surjective. Finally note that <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell,n}\to\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell,n}\to\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> factors through <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}})\to A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}})\to A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell,n})</annotation></semantics></math> factors through <math id="S5.SS2.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 5.4</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP. Hence, <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{4}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{4}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}=X_{n}\sqcup Y_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}=X_{n}\sqcup Y_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemmas <a href="#S5.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 5.2. ‣ 5.2. The tetragonal locus ‣ 5. The CKgP in genus 7 with at most 3 marked points ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> and <a href="#S5.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5.2. The tetragonal locus ‣ 5. The CKgP in genus 7 with at most 3 marked points ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>, each of these pieces has the CKgP. Note that <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{\Diamond}_{4,7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{\Diamond}_{4,7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> maps properly onto <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{4}_{7,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{4}_{7,n}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{7,n}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{7,n}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> has the CKgP. Thus the result follows by Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>(<a href="#S4.I1.i2" title="item 2 ‣ Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)-(<a href="#S4.I1.i3" title="item 3 ‣ Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4. The Chow–Künneth generation Property ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p">The next step is to show that all classes in <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell,n})</annotation></semantics></math> are restrictions from <math id="S5.SS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.5</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=2,3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, the restriction <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})\to A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})\to A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell,n})</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the following diagram:</span></p>
<table id="S5.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.E5.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="73.36" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-36.68px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 385.18 73.36" width="385.18"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,73.36) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(192.59,0) translate(0,36.68)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -192.59 -28.16)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 73.36)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 15.47)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 36.39 0) translate(49.27,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -43.31 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="72.78"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E5.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 222.37 0) translate(72.48,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -33.31 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.82em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="52.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E5.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell,n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell,n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 64.84)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(85.65,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -79.7 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10.52em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="145.56"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E5.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(\mathcal{B})[z_{1},\ldots,z_{n},\zeta_{1},\ldots,\zeta_{n}]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(\mathcal{B})[z_{1},\ldots,z_{n},\zeta_{1},\ldots,\zeta_{n}]}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 171.31 0) translate(123.54,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -84.38 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:11.2em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="154.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E5.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell})[z_{1},\ldots,z_{n},\zeta_{1},\ldots,\zeta_{n}].}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell})[z_{1},\ldots,z_{n},\zeta_{1},\ldots,\zeta_{n}].}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -57.4 24.67 L 62.16 24.67"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 62.43 24.67)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -106.94 -12.44 L -106.94 11.86"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 -106.94 12.14)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -21.01 -24.7 L 11.09 -24.7"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.37 -24.7)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 102.26 -12.44 L 102.26 11.36"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 102.26 11.64)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">The map <math id="S5.SS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{B})\to A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{B})\to A^{*}(\Sigma_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective
by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Lemma 4.2]</cite> for <math id="S5.SS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=2</annotation></semantics></math>, and by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Lemma 4.3(1)]</cite> for <math id="S5.SS2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=3</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the bottom horizontal arrow is surjective. By Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5.2. The tetragonal locus ‣ 5. The CKgP in genus 7 with at most 3 marked points ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>, the right vertical arrow is also surjective. Hence, the top horizontal arrow is surjective.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.6</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S5.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, the pullback map <math id="S5.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})\to A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})\to A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond})</annotation></semantics></math>
is surjective.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we fix some notation. Let</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{3,n}\xhookrightarrow{\jmath}Y_{n}\xhookrightarrow{\iota}\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathvariant="italic">↪</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="italic">ȷ</mo></mover><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathvariant="italic">↪</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝜄</mo></mover><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{3,n}\xhookrightarrow{\jmath}Y_{n}\xhookrightarrow{\iota}\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">denote the natural closed inclusion maps. Let <math id="S5.SS2.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\colon\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}\to(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\colon\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}\to(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the map from the top left to top right in diagram (<a href="#S5.E2" title="In 5.2. The tetragonal locus ‣ 5. The CKgP in genus 7 with at most 3 marked points ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>).
We let <math id="S5.SS2.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}:X_{n}\rightarrow(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}:X_{n}\rightarrow(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the composite of the open inclusion <math id="S5.SS2.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{n}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{n}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.SS2.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:=\phi\circ\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ι</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:=\phi\circ\iota</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S5.SS2.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be the composite of the open inclusion <math id="S5.SS2.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{2,n}\hookrightarrow Y_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{2,n}\hookrightarrow Y_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the following commutative diagram, where the bottom row is exact.</span></p>
<table id="S5.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.E6.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="74.68" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-37.34px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 389.14 74.68" width="389.14"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,74.68) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(194.57,0) translate(0,37.34)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -194.57 -28.32)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 74.67)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 15.47)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 81.14 0) translate(82.47,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -43.31 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="72.78"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E6.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 65.66)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(40.57,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -34.61 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="55.39"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E6.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*-2}(Y_{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*-2}(Y_{n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 86.17 0) translate(77.44,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -38.27 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.53em;--ltx-fo-height:0.85em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.69)" width="62.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E6.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">◇</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 212.88 0) translate(69.88,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -30.71 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="47.58"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E6.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(X_{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(X_{n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 319.42 0) translate(51.47,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -12.3 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="10.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E6.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces 0.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces 0.}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -30.96 13.07 L -30.96 -10.73"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -30.96 -11)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -46.65 -1.86)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.9em;--ltx-fo-height:0.53em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.28" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.39)" width="12.44"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E6.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -1.86 13.07 L 58.58 -12.38"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.92162 -0.3881 0.3881 0.92162 58.84 -12.49)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 31.87 5.38)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.58em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.02)" width="15.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E6.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi^{\prime*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">′</mo><mo lspace="0.222em">⁣</mo><mo mathsize="0.710em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\phi^{\prime*}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -113.16 -24.86 L -76.02 -24.86"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -75.74 -24.86)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -99.25 -20.22)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.71em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="9.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E6.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\iota_{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ι</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\iota_{*}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 13.55 -24.86 L 50.68 -24.86"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 50.96 -24.86)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 125.12 -24.86 L 157.23 -24.86"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 157.5 -24.86)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 5.2. ‣ 5.2. The tetragonal locus ‣ 5. The CKgP in genus 7 with at most 3 marked points ‣ Extensions of tautological rings and motivic structures in the cohomology of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>′</mo><mo lspace="0.222em">⁣</mo><mo>∗</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime*}</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective.
It thus suffices to show that the image of <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ι</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in the image of <math id="S5.SS2.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. To do so, we consider another commutative diagram where the bottom row is exact.</span></p>
<table id="S5.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.E7.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="74.25" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-37.12px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 402.77 74.25" width="402.77"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,74.25) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(201.39,0) translate(0,37.12)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -201.38 -28.1)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 74.24)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 15.47)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 88.67 0) translate(82.47,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -43.31 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="72.78"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E7.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}((\mathbb{P}\mathcal{E}^{\vee})^{n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 65.23)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(44.34,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -38.38 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.55em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="62.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E7.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*-1}(\Sigma_{3,n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*-1}(\Sigma_{3,n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 101.99 0) translate(69.16,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -29.99 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.33em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="46.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E7.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(Y_{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(Y_{n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 220.41 0) translate(72.92,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -33.76 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.88em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="53.68"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E7.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(\Sigma_{2,n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A^{*}(\Sigma_{2,n})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 333.05 0) translate(51.47,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -12.3 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="10.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E7.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces 0.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces 0.}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -30.24 12.86 L -30.24 -11.83"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 -30.24 -12.11)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -46.6 -2.52)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.95em;--ltx-fo-height:0.53em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.28" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.39)" width="13.11"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E7.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\psi^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ψ</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\psi^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -0.14 12.86 L 61.34 -12.17"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.92616 -0.3771 0.3771 0.92616 61.59 -12.28)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 34.11 5.38)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.17em;--ltx-fo-height:0.58em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.02)" width="16.16"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E7.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\psi^{\prime*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ψ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">′</mo><mo lspace="0.222em">⁣</mo><mo mathsize="0.710em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\psi^{\prime*}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -112.44 -24.64 L -67.02 -24.64"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -66.74 -24.64)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -94.06 -19.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.67em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="9.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E7.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\jmath_{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ȷ</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\jmath_{*}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 5.98 -24.64 L 51.4 -24.64"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 51.68 -24.64)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 131.94 -24.64 L 164.04 -24.64"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 164.32 -24.64)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g></g></svg></span></td>
